      "body_plain": "Please refer to https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-help/2005-February/066041.html\n主要的原因, 從 help file (看help file 指令: ? fisher.test) 來看:\n\n      Note this fails (with an error message) when the entries of the table\n      are too large.\n\nNote, the _entries_, not the dimensions.  The issue is how many tables\nneed to be enumerated.\n\nBrian D. Ripley 的建議是你應該用 log-linear model 來了解資料間的dependence, 然後可以藉此更了解你的data.\n\nFor anyone wants to reproduce the result:\ntable <- matrix(c(32, 153, 167, 86, 3, 5234, 13017, 4088, 883, 225, 3, 8, 1, 2, 1), 3, 5, dimnames= list(B13 = c(1:3), B14 = c(1:5)))\nfisher.test(table)\n\n如果只是想讓他動:\nfisher.test(a, simulate.p.value = TRUE, B = 20000)\n\nOn Thursday, April 25, 2013 4:18:26 AM UTC-7, 馬來糕 wrote:\n> 請教一下！\n> 先提一下.....\n> 我有一份2萬多筆的回卷資料，\n> 以spss跑卡方獨立性檢定時，\n> 發現每個cell的期望值小於5的格子數約佔33.3%，\n> 所以我改用Fisher's exact test跑資料，\n> 可是spss的報表說記憶體不足，\n> 跑不出來，\n> 用sas跑也出現同樣的問題。\n>\n> 所以我去國家高速網路與計算中心，\n> 申請了一個帳號，\n> 準備用R跑看看，\n> 我就參考TKU NET.Stat的語法去跑，\n> >if(!exists(\"chisq.test\", mode=\"function\"))\n> + library(ctest)\n> > B13 <- `101q44`$B13\n> > B14 <- `101q44`$B14\n> > xy.table <- table(B13,B14)\n> > chi <- chisq.test(xy.table)\n> > chi\n>\n>     Pearson's Chi-squared test\n>\n> data:  xy.table\n> X-squared = 453.6677, df = 8, p-value < 2.2e-16\n>\n> > chi$observed\n>   B14\n> B13     1     2     3     4     5\n>  1    32   153   167    86     3\n>  2  5234 13017  4088   883   225\n>  3     3     8     1     2     1\n>\n> 到這裡都沒問題!!!!!\n> ===================================\n>\n> 可是改用fisher's exact test時，\n> 就出現錯誤了，\n> > fi <- fisher.test(xy.table)\n> Error in fisher.test(xy.table) : Bug in FEXACT: gave negative key\n>\n> 有那位高手可以教我如何下指令嗎？\n> 謝謝！",
      "body_snippet": "Please refer to https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-help/2005-February/066041.html\n主要的原因, 從 help file (看help file 指令: ? fisher.test) 來看:\n\n      Note this fails (with an error message) when the entries of",
